  interactively, you can put into a script. This repeatability transforms individual knowledge into
  shared process.

  Modern terminals have evolved considerably. They support color, images, hyperlinks, and even
  graphical widgets. Terminal multiplexers like tmux let users split screens and persist sessions
  across connections. Remote machines feel local through SSH. The ecosystem of tools — from vim to
  git to grep — represents decades of accumulated, composable craft.

  What makes the terminal endure is not nostalgia, but fitness. It rewards investment. Learning the
  terminal is learning a language, and like any language, fluency changes how you think. For those
  who speak it, the terminal is not a limitation — it is freedom.

